    {
      "id": "p0012-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In Legends of Localization Book 1, we looked at how the original Legend of Zelda was translated into English. There was one key issue, though - the game is so old that nobody remembers who the actual translator was or how the game's translation process worked. As a result, we could see how things changed in translation, but there was no way to ask why.",
        "raw": "In Legends ofL ocalization Book 1, we\nlooked at how the original Legend\nofZ elda was translated into English.\nThere was one key issue, though\n- the game is so old that nobody\nremembers who the actual translator\nwas or how the game's translation\nprocess worked. As a result, we could\nsee how things changed in translation,\nbut there was no way to ask why.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.59804225,
          0.17193571,
          0.89503923,
          0.34966429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.5967331,
          0.17122143,
          0.89634838,
          0.35073571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          10,
          13,
          15,
          18,
          20,
          25,
          28,
          30,
          31,
          32
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "在《Legends of Localization》第1卷，我们研究了初代《The Legend of Zelda》如何译成英语。不过有个关键问题：游戏太老，已经没人记得究竟是谁翻译的，也没人记得翻译是怎么进行的。因此，我们看得见翻译改了什么，却无从追问为什么。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
